# ─── Generated by LeakLens itself ────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are scan artifacts, not source. The patch in particular contains
# credentials in CLEARTEXT by design — it must never reach a repository.
leaklens-fix.patch
*.patch
leaklens-remediation.md
leaklens.env.example
report.json
*.sarif

# ─── Secrets, defensively ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A secret scanner whose own repo leaks a credential is the worst possible look.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa
id_ed25519
credentials.json

# ─── Third-party material — must not be vendored into the repo ───────────────
# The rules forbid vendoring third-party source. mermaid.min.js lives here, and
# the hackathon's own PDF is not ours to redistribute.
tools/

# ─── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reproducible-build artifacts are rebuilt by `node build.mjs`; the two hashes
# are published in README.md rather than the binaries being committed.
dist/

# ─── Docs: ship the prep notes, not the generated PDFs ───────────────────────
# The Markdown prep research is deliberate pre-kickoff work the rules permit,
# and committing it makes the AI-assisted process transparent rather than hidden.
# The PDFs are generated from that Markdown, and are stale.
docs/*
!docs/prep/
docs/prep/*
!docs/prep/*.md

# ─── Scratch / local ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.golden/
.new-*.js
.splice.mjs
*.tmp
*.bak
*.original.md

# ─── Node / tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# ─── Editor / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
*.swp
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
